The original LICENSE and source attribution are preserved.

LocalDrop modifications include the application name and identifiers,
the original LocalDrop icon, a Linux AirDrop process bridge and user
interface, and fork-specific release automation and documentation.

AirDrop integration invokes separately installed programs. Their source
repositories, pinned revisions and licenses are documented under
support/airdrop. They retain their own licenses and attribution:
  omdrop-plugin: https://github.com/brentkearney/omdrop-plugin (MIT)
  omdrop-awdl: https://github.com/brentkearney/omdrop-awdl (GPL-2.0-only)
  OWL: https://github.com/jedbillyb/owl (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  radiotap-library: https://github.com/radiotap/radiotap-library (ISC)
  omdrop-owl: https://github.com/t4t5/omdrop-owl

LocalDrop is not affiliated with LocalSend or Apple. AirDrop is an Apple
trademark. The upstream radio implementation is experimental and its
hardware-specific limitations apply to LocalDrop's AirDrop feature.
